You copy the scaler's type and metadata from the KEDA specification into the rule (type into custom.type, metadata into custom.metadata, or the --scale-rule-* CLI options). Then KEDA:
• polls the source every 30 seconds (the polling interval doesn't apply to HTTP and TCP rules);
• computes desiredReplicas = ceil(current metric value ÷ target value), capped by the maximum;
• scales out in steps of 1, 4, 8, 16, 32 and so on, with no scale-up stabilization window;
• scales in only after the condition has held for the 300-second scale-down stabilization window, and then removes all the replicas that need to go;
• waits a 300-second cool down period after the last event before the final step from one replica to zero. In multiple revision mode, adding a rule creates a new revision, and older revisions keep their old rules.

